From: Charles <charles05@canonical.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 16:31:59 +0100
Subject: tests: make temp-dir cleanup non-fatal

Forwarded: not-needed

prepare-test-environment.sh removes its temporary dir in an EXIT trap under
'set -e'. Session helpers spawned by the test (xdg-desktop-portal,
xdg-permission-store, pipewire, wireplumber) may still be creating sockets in
XDG_RUNTIME_DIR when the trap fires, so rm -rf can race them and exit non-zero
("Directory not empty"). That aborts the wrapper and marks an otherwise
successful run as failed. Retry the removal once after a short settle, and
never let cleanup failure fail the test.
---
 tests/prepare-test-environment.sh | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/prepare-test-environment.sh b/tests/prepare-test-environment.sh
index 1ec70ae..4252bc4 100755
--- a/tests/prepare-test-environment.sh
+++ b/tests/prepare-test-environment.sh
@@ -3,7 +3,11 @@
 set -xe
 
 tmpdir=$(mktemp -d --tmpdir g-r-d-tests-XXXXXX)
-trap '{ rm -rf $tmpdir; }' EXIT
+# Cleanup must never fail the test: session helpers (xdg-desktop-portal,
+# pipewire, wireplumber, ...) may still be creating sockets under
+# XDG_RUNTIME_DIR when the trap runs, which makes 'rm -rf' race them and exit
+# non-zero ("Directory not empty"). Retry once, then ignore the result.
+trap '{ rm -rf "$tmpdir" 2>/dev/null || { sleep 1; rm -rf "$tmpdir" 2>/dev/null; } || true; }' EXIT
 
 export HOME="$tmpdir/home"
 export XDG_RUNTIME_DIR="$tmpdir/xrd"
